<article class="env-lemma" id="0844">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0844">Lemma <span data-tag="0844">71.7.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $f \in \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is a regular section, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any $x \in X$ the image $f \in \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is not a zerodivisor. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any affine $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ étale over $X$ the restriction $f|_ U$ is a nonzerodivisor of $A$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X$ such that $f|_ U$ is a regular section of $\mathcal{O}_ U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>